 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Stage 1 takes 5.5 hours on a single A100 for 100,000 iterations. Stage 2 takes 6.5 hours on a single A100 for 100,000 iterations [S1].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Depends on the size of the Zip-NeRF hash grid and the Fast Cache. Zip-NeRF uses a sparse structure, reducing memory compared to dense grids. Fast Cache uses 64 secondary rays for estimation and 16 for the NeRF-cache control variate [S1].
-*   **Strengths:** Reduces bias in radiance caching by using a control variate (Fast Cache). Joint training allows for consistent optimization of material and environment [S1].
-*   **Limitations:** Requires significant GPU time (12+ hours total for full training). Relies on the quality of the initial Zip-NeRF cache [S1].
